NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY DATA, MODELS AND LIBRARIES — THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE COVERS
THE SOURCE CODE OF THIS PROJECT ONLY.

Files in this repository that come from other sources, and all data fetched
from other providers at runtime, are owned by their respective sources. They
are NOT licensed under MIT and remain subject to their own licenses and terms.
In particular:

  - JPL ephemerides and lunar orientation (web/data/de440s.bsp,
    web/data/moon_pa_de440_200625.bpc, web/data/eph/, kernels/): NASA/JPL NAIF
    DE440 products.
  - Earth orientation tables (web/data/earth_orient.json): IAU 2000A nutation
    coefficients and Delta-T / leap-second tables taken from Skyfield / ERFA
    (IERS data).
  - Lunar terrain (web/data/site_dem.json) and lunar textures: NASA LRO/LOLA,
    NASA SVS CGI Moon Kit (U.S. public domain).
  - Launch pads (web/data/pads.json): The Space Devs, Launch Library 2.
  - Historical orbit summary (web/data/gecmis.json): derived from public
    CelesTrak data via github.com/jtmiclat/celestrak-historical (MIT). Only
    derived summaries are distributed; no raw TLEs and no Space-Track data.
  - Asteroid shape models (web/models/ast/*.glb): NASA PDS Small Bodies Node
    (public domain); the source of each model is listed in
    web/models/ast/katalog.json.
  - DAMIT asteroid shapes and spin states (web/models/ast/damit/): Creative
    Commons Attribution 4.0 — Durech, J., Sidorin, V., Kaasalainen, M. 2010,
    A&A 513, A46; each model rests on its own publication listed in DAMIT.
  - Satellite models (web/models/sats/): NASA 3D Resources and NASA Eyes on
    the Earth (NASA/JPL-Caltech visualization models).
  - Vehicle and launch models (web/models/lander.glb, orb.glb, stage.glb,
    web/models/rockets/): derived from NASA 3D Resources (public domain).
  - Planet textures (web/textures/planets/): Solar System Scope, CC BY 4.0
    (Mercury to Neptune, Saturn's rings); Pluto: NASA/JHUAPL/SwRI New Horizons
    (PIA19956, public domain). Other images under web/textures/ are not
    covered by the MIT grant either.
  - Libraries (web/lib/, pylib/): three.js, satellite.js, Motion, NumberFlow,
    torph, jplephem (MIT) and Clarabel (Apache-2.0). Their license texts sit
    next to them (web/lib/*.LICENSE.md, web/lib/clarabel/, pylib/).
  - Development skills (.claude/skills/): MIT, see .claude/skills/LICENSES.md.

The NASA name, logo and insignia (which also appear on some model textures)
are subject to NASA's usage guidelines. Use of NASA material does not imply
NASA endorsement of this project.

Exception: the satellite family models in web/models/fam/ were made for this
project and are MIT, like the code.

Live sources fetched at runtime (CelesTrak, JPL Horizons, JPL SBDB, JPL
Sentry, JPL CAD, NASA GIBS, NASA Moon Trek, Esri World Imagery, AWS Terrain
Tiles, EOX Sentinel-2 cloudless, Open-Meteo) are used under each provider's
terms. Some restrict commercial or high-volume use: Esri World Imagery
requires on-screen attribution and is subject to Esri's terms of use;
Sentinel-2 cloudless is CC BY-SA 4.0 with on-screen attribution; AWS Terrain
Tiles carry their source attributions (USGS 3DEP, SRTM, GMTED2010, ETOPO1 and
others); and Open-Meteo's free API is for non-commercial use.

In short: the MIT grant does not extend to any third-party data, model,
texture or library. See "Veri kaynakları ve lisanslar" in README.md for the
per-source summary, and remove anything whose terms do not fit your use.

